data.content:
Done. Here's what changed and how to use it:

**`Clock.cs`** — static helper backed by `AsyncLocal<T>`, so parallel tests can't interfere with each other. Production cost is one null-check per call.

**`InvoiceCalculator.cs`** now reads `Clock.UtcNow` instead of `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow`.

### Usage in tests

```csharp
[Fact]
public void IsOverdue_WhenPastDue_ReturnsTrue()
{
    var dueDate = new DateTimeOffset(2025, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);

    using var _ = Clock.Override(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));

    Assert.True(new InvoiceCalculator().IsOverdue(dueDate));
}
```

The `using` block scopes the override — time resets automatically when the test ends. No DI, no interfaces, no packages needed.
